## 2026-08-23T03:30–03:42+08:00 — resolved live-run failures and authoritative outputs

The first attempts exposed environment/process coordination failures; they are retained here with their exact errors rather than hidden:

```text
Error: Windows(Calibration(Calibration(RoundTripTooLong { round_trip_us: 148597, maximum_us: 20000 })))
```

The first saturated attempt, with the large transfer started before calibration, produced:

```text
calibration sequence=0 round_trip_us=19231 offset_us=552234 error_bound_us=9615 instability_warning=false
calibration sequence=1 round_trip_us=18970 offset_us=555133 error_bound_us=9485 instability_warning=false
Error: Windows(Calibration(Calibration(RoundTripTooLong { round_trip_us: 30940, maximum_us: 20000 })))
```

These were genuine calibration-environment failures: the tool's unchanged calibration gate rejects a sample above its exact 20,000 us maximum. A concurrently running canonical installed client and stale orphaned `parec` processes from other live attempts were also observed and cleaned without changing the Scheduled Task or firewall. The authoritative saturated run started the load only after the diagnostic session was ready, allowing calibration to complete, and then completed with a reading.

